    // ── Within-tier precision floors: a "q4" tier that is partly q8 ──────────────────────────────────
    // These are the sharpest cases in the ledger. The user selects q4 and gets q8 weights for part of
    // the model, decided inside the provider where neither the worker's tier resolver nor its quality
    // rank can see it. Declared here so the substitution is at least visible — but declaring is not
    // reconciling: SC-16025 owns the actual defect, which is that `effective_quant_label`, the asset
    // record and the evidence cell all still describe such a run as a plain "q4". Same class as the
    // sc-11042 NVFP4 and sc-12425 int8-convrot aliasing, and the cost here is already measured, so
    // SC-16025 is about the invisibility rather than the size.
    {
      "model": "mage_flow_base",
      "component": "textEncoder",
      "residentTier": "q8",
      "appliesToTiers": ["q4"],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "An 8-bit FLOOR on the Qwen3-VL LM's 36 decoder layers: a q4 request is silently raised to 8 bits for them, so the q4 tier shares q8's decoder layers and differs only in the token embedding and the vision tower.",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costGb": 1.9,
        "source": "crates/media/mlx-gen/mlx-gen-mage/src/quant.rs `LM_LAYER_MIN_BITS = 8`; the cost is recorded in mlx-gen-mage/src/memory.rs (q4 calibration peak 5.940 → 7.868 GB, of which the LM's 36 layers at 8 bits are ~1.9 GB) and in the manifest's per-tier TE footprints (q4 4.331 vs q8 4.731 GB on disk)."
      }
    },
    {
      "model": "mage_flow_base",
      "component": "transformerHead",
      "residentTier": "q8",
      "appliesToTiers": ["q4"],
      "backends": ["mlx"],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "An 8-bit floor on the DiT's `norm_out.linear` (the final modulation projection), which q4 cannot serve without visible degradation — a uniformly-Q4 head is what made the Q4 tier render a repeating tiled texture (sc-15071).",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costGb": 0.009,
        "source": "crates/media/mlx-gen/mlx-gen-mage/src/quant.rs `FINAL_MOD_MIN_BITS = 8` — the floor is applied by the single seam `floor_bits(FINAL_MOD_BASE, bits)` that final_layer.rs:54 and convert.rs:172 both call, with no model or variant branch; quant.rs records the cost as \"Keeping it packed at 8 bits costs 18.9 MB against 10.6 MB at Q4\". The manifest's per-tier DiT footprints record q4 2.317 → 2.326 GB.",
        "note": "MLX LANE ONLY, and that is not an oversight: candle-gen-mage has no floor symbol at all — its transformer.rs passes the requested `quant` straight through to `final_mod` — so on the candle lane a q4 render really is uniformly q4 here. That asymmetry is a separate finding from this ledger's scope; SC-16025 owns the label reconciliation and should carry it."
      }
    },
