    // ── SenseNova-U1: a unified model whose dense heads the first audit missed ────────────────────────
    // All six entries host q4/q8/bf16, and BOTH lanes state that the token embedding, `lm_head`, the
    // flow-matching head and the vision embedders stay dense in every tier. There is no separate VAE or
    // text encoder to declare on this family, which is exactly how it fell through the first pass.
    //
    // ONE ROW PER LANE (second sc-15799 review). The lanes hold these components at DIFFERENT
    // precisions: mlx-gen keeps them at the checkpoint's bf16 store dtype, while candle-gen widens the
    // two vision conv kernels and `fm_head` to **f32** (`candle-gen-sensenova/src/quant.rs::get_f32`,
    // sc-14249) so every dense leaf it multiplies against an f32 activation shares one dtype. A single
    // both-lanes row could only be wrong in one direction or the other, so the checker's uniqueness key
    // is (model, component, lane) and each lane declares its own `residentTier`. The unmeasured amnesty
    // stays keyed on (model, component), so splitting does not widen it.
    {
      "model": "sensenova_u1_8b",
      "component": "transformerHead",
      "residentTier": "bf16",
      "appliesToTiers": [
        "q4",
        "q8"
      ],
      "backends": [
        "mlx"
      ],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "The Qwen3 backbone is packed but the token embedding, `lm_head` and the flow-matching `fm_head` stay dense bf16 in every tier under mlx-gen — the tier author's split, which the packer follows rather than overrides. (the base entry.)",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "unmeasured",
        "source": "crates/media/mlx-gen/mlx-gen-sensenova/src/convert.rs — \"a 2-D dense target (`embed_tokens` / `lm_head` / `fm_head`) is never packed\"; crates/media/mlx-gen/mlx-gen-sensenova/src/quant.rs — \"Everything else stays dense in every tier: the token embedding, `lm_head`, ... the flow-matching `fm_head`, and the timestep/noise-scale embedders\". MLX holds them at the checkpoint's bf16 store dtype; it does not widen (the only f32 in the MLX vision path is a transient positional-embedding cast that is immediately cast back to the input dtype).",
        "owedBy": "sc-16015",
        "note": "ADDED by the sc-15799 review, which found all six SenseNova-U1 entries undeclared. ADJUDICATION: U1 is a unified MoT model with \"no separate VAE or text encoder\", so the ledger's diffusion vocabulary does not map cleanly — but that is a naming problem, not a reason to omit. The dense matmul targets ARE declarable under this file's threshold (they are `[out, in]` Linears a packer could take, and the packer deliberately skips them), so they are declared: `transformerHead` for `embed_tokens` / `lm_head` / `fm_head`, `visionTower` for the two Conv vision embedders. The dense RMSNorms, QK-norms and timestep/noise-scale embedders are NOT declared — they are per-channel vectors, which the threshold excludes for every model. UNMEASURED because no isolated figure exists: the tree records only whole-model numbers (~70.5 GB peak on candle, ~11 GB packed-q4 on MLX) and the packed set (\"588 triples, the ~16.2 B parameters\"), and deriving a component split from vocab_size x hidden_size would be inventing evidence. Amnestied as a pre-existing residency the audit MISSED. SPLIT PER LANE by the second sc-15799 review, which found the single both-lanes row UNDER-DECLARED candle. The two ports make independent dtype decisions and the ledger's uniqueness key is now (model, component, lane), so each lane states its own residentTier instead of one of them being wrong. Declaring bf16 for both would have under-declared candle; declaring f32 for both would have over-declared mlx. MLX lane: bf16, the checkpoint's store dtype. The candle sibling row declares f32 for the same component because candle-gen widens it — see that row."
      }
    },
