        "owedBy": "sc-16015",
        "note": "ADDED by the sc-15799 review, which found all six SenseNova-U1 entries undeclared. ADJUDICATION: U1 is a unified MoT model with \"no separate VAE or text encoder\", so the ledger's diffusion vocabulary does not map cleanly — but that is a naming problem, not a reason to omit. The dense matmul targets ARE declarable under this file's threshold (they are `[out, in]` Linears a packer could take, and the packer deliberately skips them), so they are declared: `transformerHead` for `embed_tokens` / `lm_head` / `fm_head`, `visionTower` for the two Conv vision embedders. The dense RMSNorms, QK-norms and timestep/noise-scale embedders are NOT declared — they are per-channel vectors, which the threshold excludes for every model. UNMEASURED because no isolated figure exists: the tree records only whole-model numbers (~70.5 GB peak on candle, ~11 GB packed-q4 on MLX) and the packed set (\"588 triples, the ~16.2 B parameters\"), and deriving a component split from vocab_size x hidden_size would be inventing evidence. Amnestied as a pre-existing residency the audit MISSED. SPLIT PER LANE by the second sc-15799 review, which found the single both-lanes row UNDER-DECLARED candle. The two ports make independent dtype decisions and the ledger's uniqueness key is now (model, component, lane), so each lane states its own residentTier instead of one of them being wrong. Declaring bf16 for both would have under-declared candle; declaring f32 for both would have over-declared mlx. CANDLE lane: f32, because `fm_head` is widened by `quant::get_f32`. `embed_tokens` and `lm_head` ride the bf16 store dtype on this lane, so f32 is the component's UPPER resident precision — the tier the row must declare, since the invariant is one-directional about being ABOVE the selected tier. The mlx sibling row declares bf16."
